         "label": "PL - FAQ",
         "name": "module_9",
         "params": {
          "items": [
           {
            "answer": "<p>Yes. HPMC (hydroxypropyl methylcellulose) vegetarian capsules are available across all our standard sizes. They are plant-derived, kosher, and halal compatible. Cost is slightly higher than gelatin but most brands targeting health-conscious audiences choose vegetarian as a default.</p>",
            "question": "Do you offer vegetarian capsules?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "<p>Standard gelatin capsules are derived from bovine sources, so they are not appropriate for vegetarian or kosher/halal positioning unless verified. HPMC capsules avoid this entirely. Both formats can be manufactured allergen-free for the top common allergens (soy, dairy, wheat, etc.) with proper segregation, which is part of our standard GMP practice.</p>",
            "question": "What are common allergens to watch for in capsules?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "<p>Most capsule formulations have a 24-month shelf life from manufacture date when stored under standard conditions. Specific shelf life depends on the active ingredients. Stability testing for longer claims (36 months) is available on request.</p>",
            "question": "What is the typical shelf life of a private label capsule product?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We offer delayed-release (enteric-coated) capsules for ingredients that need to bypass stomach acid, and controlled-release formats for ingredients where extended absorption matters. These are scoped during the formulation phase based on the specific actives.</p>",
            "question": "Can you do controlled-release or delayed-release capsules?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "<p>Both gelatin and HPMC capsules come in a wide range of colors, including clear, opaque, and two-tone combinations. Capsule printing (brand name or logo directly on the capsule) is available for orders above our standard run minimum. Talk to our team about your brand requirements.</p>",
            "question": "What color and printing options are available for capsules?"
           }
          ],
